    "sourceWikitext": "__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Cheese recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Russia|Cuisine of Russia]]\n\n'''Sirniki''' are Russian sweet curd fritters, generally eaten after the main course at dinner, but sometimes also at breakfast.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 500 [[Cookbook:g|grams]] [[Cookbook:Cottage Cheese|cottage cheese]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]s\n* 6 [[Cookbook:tablespoon|tablespoon]]s [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n\n===Garnish===\n* [[Cookbook:Sour cream|Sour cream]] and sugar or [[Cookbook:Jam|jam]], confiture.\n* [[Cookbook:Apple sauce|Apple sauce]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Mix cottage cheese, eggs, flour, sugar and salt.\n# Take piece of paste, make round, flat shape and put on warm frying pan with oil or melted butter.\n# Wait until it becomes gold colour and flip.\n# When it is brown on both sides you can eat it.\n\n== See also ==\n\n* [[Cookbook:Vareniki]]\n[[ru:Рецепт:Сырники]]\n[[Category:Russian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Pan fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for fritters|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using applesauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cottage cheese]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fruit preserves]]",
